{"id":"tam-0001","lang":"tam","tier":0,"domain":1,"text_native":"வணக்கம்","text_romanized":"vaṇakkam","text_english":"Hello","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The greeting, the reply to a greeting, AND the farewell — one word does all three. Shown once, not three times: duplicating the same string is noise, and the fact that it does three jobs belongs here rather than in three rows.","exchange_id":"tam-x0001","exchange_turn":1,"caution":"There is no neutral 'you' and no neutral greeting in everyday Tamil. The plain form is used between intimates; a stranger or an elder needs the honorific form, which is not in this set yet. Until it is, plain วัสดี is the safer default — slightly informal, never rude.","source":{"class":"authored","id":"LangKraft editorial","url":null,"licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"corroborating_sentences":[11036634]},"failure_flags":[]}
